1 // Number of lines
////////////////// 
////////////////// New line [1]
////////////////// 
1 // Type of line [1: Mooring, 2: Towing, 3:Tensor]
2 // Tension model [1: symmetric, 2: tension-only]
11 // Number of nodes used to divide catenary i
1 // Order of the elements of catenary i
120.0 // Length of catenary i [m]
50.0 // Weight over water of catenary i (kg/m)    
0.09 // Diameter of the section of catenary i [m]
0 // Flag for axial stiffness [n=0: constant axial stiffness (next line must contain EA), n=1: variable axial stiffness polynomial , n>1 : variable axial stiffness interpolated]
1.0E+07 // Youngs module multiplied by the Area for catenary i [N]
0.002 // Coefficient of the internal damping coefficient as function of EA [Azcona-2016] for i
0.0 // Coefficient of seabed static friction for i  
3.8 // Hydrodynamic Mass Coefficient for catenary i (needed for the dynamic model only)  
2.5 // Normal Drag Coefficient for catenary i (needed for the dynamic model only)  
0.5 // Tangential Drag Coefficient for catenary i (needed for the dynamic model only)  
1.0E+06 // Ground Normal stiffness for catenary i (needed for the dynamic model only) [Palm-2013b]  
0.1 // Fraction of critical damping of ground for catenary i (needed for the dynamic model only) [Palm-2013b]  
1 // Floor Id assigned to this line [from dataSeaFloor.dat]
2 // BCP index of the node with index N (Fairlead 1)
1 // BCP index of node with index 1 [IMPORTANT, THIS SHOULD BE THE LOWER ONE] (Anchor 1)
1 // Smoothstep flag
0 // Friction model [0: No friction, 1:Isotropic stick and slip, 2:Anisotropic stick and slip (used for inclined plane)]
0.01 // Limit velocity to pass from stick to slip (m/s) ONLY FOR STICK SLIP
0.6 // Static friction tangential coefficient [Used in flat floor or at the tangential direction in other floor]
0.4 // Static friction normal coefficient
0.3 // Dynamic friction coefficient
0.03 // Maximum displacement (m) ONLY FOR STICK SLIP [around Diameter/10]
